  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic Specialist Advice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT engages specialist economic advice to inform Australia&apos;s response to emerging and complex policy issues for the Indo-Pacific region. This advice helps to guide Australia&#x2019;s understanding of, and engagement with, multilateral development banks including analysis of bank reforms, membership dynamics, and achieving gender and climate outcomes at scale. It helps to inform the department on pressing issues for the region including economic development opportunities and challenges, debt distress and vulnerability, and sustainable development finance needs, as it navigates and recovers from the impacts of the polycrises.

We draw on expertise in the design and delivery of innovative development finance instruments including private investment partnerships in support of Australia&#x2019;s traditional development assistance flows. 

The total value of the investment is AUD2,500,000 over 4 years.</narrative>
  </description>
